title POST SSE - Input, Output and Closing (pending implementation)
actor "mate-service" as Client
participant "Events application" as API
participant "Bound execution" as Run
participant "Request response" as Response
database "Session / Events" as DB

== 1. Accept a message ==
Client -> API : POST user.message
API -> Response : reserve and bind
API -> DB : atomic admission + receipt
DB --> API : accepted event / fixed target
API -> Response : enqueue complete receipt
API -> Run : start after commit
Response --> Client : user.message
Run -> Response : matching preview / full events
Response --> Client : agent.*

== 2. Close the bound segment ==
alt Actual finish
  Run -> DB : commit terminal + Session idle
  DB --> Run : authoritative idle
  Run -> Response : matching idle
  Response --> Client : idle, then EOF
else Wait for tool confirmation
  Run -> DB : commit Tool Call + confirming\nSession stays running
  Run -> Response : Tool Call + confirming idle
  Response --> Client : complete events, then EOF
  Client -> API : new confirmation POST
  API -> DB : claim pending tool + resume segment
  DB --> API : committed confirmation
  API -> Response : new bound response; receipt first
  API -> Run : consume committed decision once
  Run -> DB : persist resume output
  API -> DB : read fixed segment if remote
  DB --> API : complete events
  API -> Response : matching output and idle
  Response --> Client : confirmation, output, idle, EOF
end

== 3. Independent interrupt response ==
ref over Client,DB
Interrupt uses a separate response bound to the original message.
See Database Interrupt Delivery for cross-instance handoff.
Original output stays on its original response.
end ref

== 4. Transport loss ==
Client -> API : GET Events for reconciliation
API -> DB : committed complete history
DB --> API : ordered page
API --> Client : ResultBean history
note over Client,Response
No terminal received means uncertain, not successful.
Detach only the failed response; do not replay POST.
end note
