@startuml target_decision_consumption_state
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java 74f1b8314c9a5eb3d1659dfed2ab90b787dd647f.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/ToolConfirmationState.java
' Existing symbols: PENDING, CLAIMED, COMPLETED.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository.java
' Existing symbol: markTerminal, with Session/execution locking and terminal commit.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeExecutionControlMapper.xml
' Existing symbols: claimConfirmation, claimPlanConfirmation, claimQuestionAnswer, markTerminal.
' Observed behavior: terminal execution blocks new claims but leaves unclaimed decisions PENDING.
' Pending implementation: CANCELED closes unclaimed decisions in the successful terminal transaction.
' Design reason: preserve accepted user facts while making abandoned consumption explicit.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F4F7FB
  BorderColor #42576E
  ArrowColor #42576E
}
title Accepted Decisions - Consumption State (pending implementation)
top to bottom direction

state PENDING
state CLAIMED
state COMPLETED
state CANCELED #FCE8DD

[*] --> PENDING : accepted decision committed
PENDING --> CLAIMED : claim wins while execution is RUNNING\nand stop_event_id is NULL
CLAIMED --> COMPLETED : acknowledge processing
PENDING --> CANCELED : root execution enters TERMINAL\nin the same transaction
COMPLETED --> [*]
CANCELED --> [*]

note left of PENDING
  STOPPING alone keeps PENDING.
  Rollback keeps the previous state.
  A confirming segment is not a root terminal.
end note

note right of CANCELED
  All three decision tables share this rule.
  Match session_id + execution_id.
  claimed_at remains NULL.
  completed_at equals root terminal_at.
  done / failed / terminated all close pending rows.
end note

legend bottom
  Terminal handling never rewrites CLAIMED or COMPLETED.
  Accepted user events and committed mode changes remain intact.
  Internal consumption state adds no public HTTP field or event.
endlegend
@enduml
